All project instructions live in AGENTS.md at the repo root. Read it before doing anything.

Project: VayuSetu — federated air-quality intelligence for India. Detects pollution
hotspots that official monitoring networks miss, forecasts AQI spikes 72h ahead,
attributes likely sources, and lets any Indian city import another city's model.

Key files:
  AGENTS.md                 entry point, tech stack, the seven rules
  plan.md                   full design rationale
  docs/DATA_CONTRACTS.md    frozen interfaces — read before touching any boundary
  BACKLOG.md                task list, pick the topmost unblocked item
  .claude/agents/*.md       role prompts (frontmatter is metadata; body is portable)
  .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md procedures with gotchas

Stack: Python 3.11 + FastAPI on Cloud Run, BigQuery, Firestore, LightGBM on Vertex AI,
Earth Engine, Gemini 2.5, React 18 + TypeScript + Vite, Google Maps JS + deck.gl.
Do not substitute these. Do not add a dependency for what an existing one already does.

The two rules most often broken:
  1. Model A must use leave-one-station-out cross-validation. Never train_test_split —
     a random split leaks badly and reports a fake R² above 0.95.
  2. Citizen photos raise a cell's confidence score. They never set a PM2.5 value and
     never trigger an authority alert on their own. Untrusted input, trust boundary.

Never wire alerts to real people's contact details, in any environment, including tests.
Never overclaim: this is federated model sharing (not federated learning with DP), and
a wind-sector cone (not HYSPLIT back-trajectory modelling).
